{
 "_doc": [
  "Per-chassis orientation corrections, applied by export-roster.py.",
  "",
  "MEASURED PER CHASSIS. Forward comes from the vector between the CHEST and",
  "the SPINE of the robot pose, which points forward whatever the model is",
  "called and however its parts are labelled.",
  "",
  "The turn is the NEGATION of that reading. An earlier version applied a flat",
  "180 to every chassis that read as 'backwards', which was wrong for any that",
  "were not exactly backwards: a body measuring -91 became +89, which is a bot",
  "facing left. Rounding a measurement to a convenient number throws the",
  "measurement away.",
  "",
  "`turn` spends the rotation across the fold, so the vehicle keeps the facing",
  "it has and only the robot end moves."
 ],
